[{:db/id "q-38182/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "a0810cfc-2716-503e-8eda-9bd7b08acab6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38182/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "40bf93a9-0e1a-5d27-a8f0-f3f34430aa2c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38182/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "ce492c35-85b8-5d30-8cc7-1882be5a74c4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38182/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "1453c279-fab3-529d-aaba-4443449a3b23" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38182/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "bb4ba432-2a8f-5769-8c7b-3bf2be07a4ff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38182/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "84ed8533-f1fb-5df4-95a9-e6288fd5e96f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-38182/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-38182/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-38182/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-38182/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-38182/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-38182/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38182" :question/id #uuid "4646eada-04b7-5167-b329-286673c2150b" :question/math-academy-id "q-38182" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $Q$ given below?\n\n- $Q$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $Q$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(Q)=-5$\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}|+6|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-3(8-14)+6(5-8) \\\\  & =0-3\\cdot (-6)+6\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =18-18 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(Q)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-38182/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38182"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-69835/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "6e085f7b-0c2c-5722-a81a-b58d2ccc6378" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69835/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "c17c4262-3741-5971-8718-46285875ae7c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69835/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "2e477060-5780-5268-920e-a662bc571646" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69835/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "07377c51-5e4f-5116-9e6c-1c1e54ce83f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69835/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "f9a5cd36-8ea4-56de-ace8-5b8128edfb13" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69835/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b828eb5-1cb6-5083-bcd2-dee4ad1a5979" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-69835/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-69835/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-69835/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-69835/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-69835/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-69835/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-69835" :question/id #uuid "0582f249-3bf5-5079-8fe1-8ed6df521a52" :question/math-academy-id "q-69835" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $T$ given below?\n\n- $T$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(T)=-3$\n- $T$ is **not** a singular matrix\n\n \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(2+3)-2(1+6)-1(-1+4) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 7-1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =20-14-3 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(T)=3\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-69835/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-69835"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-280403/field-1/56c57502ed9362f3f416b4398e79545a0252f6594946b2d60ff940ea8bef1e7b" :answer/id #uuid "190df470-cb21-5f5f-a0c6-768f6bd8a7f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "44" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280403/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0319ad1-03eb-5a51-a67c-e55d25763f00" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280403/field-1/56c57502ed9362f3f416b4398e79545a0252f6594946b2d60ff940ea8bef1e7b" :answer-field/choices ["q-280403/field-1/56c57502ed9362f3f416b4398e79545a0252f6594946b2d60ff940ea8bef1e7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280403" :question/id #uuid "2bd2a270-0e48-5ebe-b1ab-9a18fb1a3719" :question/math-academy-id "q-280403" :question/problem "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & x & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $det(A)=37$, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(F) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & x & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}x & 4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}3 & x \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(x\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 5)-(3\\cdot 1-4\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =2(x-20)-(3+8) \\\\  & =2x-40-11 \\\\  & =2x-51\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $37,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-51 & =37 \\\\ 2x & =88 \\\\ x & =44.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-280403/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280403"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-280519/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "2fad3e84-073e-5dca-b865-a32ab83df94c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280519/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "e9f9fcf0-4f20-5133-908f-a1dbf85066a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280519/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e1bfaa7-81e3-5dbc-937a-0178c987a77c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280519/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer-field/choices ["q-280519/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-280519/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280519" :question/id #uuid "0fc67642-4c1a-5d0b-9b18-c66e38eea3ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-280519" :question/problem "Given that $G=[\\begin{aligned}x & 2x-1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & x+1 & -4\\end{aligned}]$ is singular, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 2x-1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & x+1 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ x+1 & -4\\end{aligned}|-(2x-1)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}|+6|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & x+1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x(3\\cdot (-4)-0\\cdot (x+1))-(2x-1)(0)+6(0\\cdot (x+1)-3\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =x(-12)+0+6(3) \\\\  & =-12x+18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12x+18 & =0 \\\\ -12x & =-18 \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-280519/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280519"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-280541/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "698fa493-2d03-50fd-bb8f-c1c8495b2b59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280541/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "96a1507d-0f5f-57d6-932f-9cdcdc22b501" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280541/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer-field/choices ["q-280541/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280541/field-2/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "6773640e-8024-5910-b766-bb433bbcf121" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280541/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf5590f5-597e-5e73-a790-25380b0453cd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280541/field-2/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer-field/choices ["q-280541/field-2/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280541" :question/id #uuid "5f431d5d-b965-53ac-8681-9fb78bb22b04" :question/math-academy-id "q-280541" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of $[\\begin{aligned}x & 2x & 5 \\\\ 3 & x & 4 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ is $40$, find all the possible values of $x$ **in ascending order**.\n\nIn ascending order, $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let’s use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 2x & 5 \\\\ 3 & x & 4 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x|\\begin{aligned}x & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2x|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}|+5|\\begin{aligned}3 & x \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x(2x-4)-2x(3\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 7)+5(3-7x) \\\\  & =x(2x-4)-2x(-22)+15-35x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-4x+44x+15-35x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+5x+15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $40$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+5x+15 & =40 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+5x-25 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{-5\\pm \\sqrt{{5}^{2}-4(2)(-25)}}{2(2)} \\\\ x & =\\frac{-5+\\sqrt{225}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5\\pm 15}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, **in ascending order**, the solutions are $x=-5$ and $x=\\frac{5}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-280541/field-1" "q-280541/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280541"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
